From 423edc4d4a910139e66cb340a5510738ee454042 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:17:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] state(v2): decode the legacy coin wire in every coin codec

EncodeCoin writes a legacy coin as its LegacyCoinWire (T1-06), but only
the sparse-state decoder read it, with its own parser; the fast-sync
utxoshard decoder and the disk-state decoder accepted V2 output frames
only. A legacy coin therefore failed to decode in a utxoshard message
(peers were discouraged with bad-utxoshard and p2p_ecash_state_sync never
completed its swarm).

Add DecodeCoinOutput, the inverse of EncodeCoinOutput (canonical
CompactSize, at most MAX_LEGACY_COIN_SCRIPT_BYTES, no trailing byte), and
use it in all three decoders, bounding the coin frame by
MAX_COIN_OUTPUT_BYTES.

Tests (coin_legacy_bit_tests): the state coin round trip also decodes the
bare coin wire and carries the coins through a utxoshard message; the
legacy coin wire decodes only in its canonical form.

Rebase onto coordinator 276 (81e8ef1774): the coordinator's UTXO
statistics (kernel/coinstats.cpp TxOutSer) encoded each coin with
EncodeOutput, which refuses a legacy coin, so gettxoutsetinfo failed once a
legacy coin existed. It now writes the coin wire (EncodeCoinOutput).

Tier: V2

Coordinator integration provenance (reference405):
0001-resolved-legacy-coin-cost.patch: Same-purpose introduced defect; original named owner retained.
All60 authored input payloads retained, with prerequisite-aware same-purpose splits; distinct legacy-index and inherited CXX compatibility remain independent. Pre-format source equals exact403+all60 control tree95718fceff83364b74294a751bd752b2f1a4e384. Only pinnedRuff import/format cleanup follows. Original author commands/hashes are historical reference evidence, not combined405 approval. Reference OFF/native/Rust full gates are preserved separately; combined compile/runtime NOT_RUN.
